WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.120
- [Kris Maher] I've been in
East Palestine this week,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.310
talking to residents who
were forced to evacuate

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.740
after a derailment of a
Norfolk Southern train

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.243
on February 3rd.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.330
Residents were told that
they could return home.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.530
But since they've been back,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.780
many have concerns about
being back in their homes,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.580
and they're concerned about smells

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.833
and the potential for health effects

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:22.500
from chemicals that were
released during the derailment.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.340
Right now, there's sort of,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.620
just this kind of cloud of concern

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.221
that's hanging over the town.
(wind chimes ring)

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:29.670
(soft staccato music)

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.310
On Friday, February 3rd, around 9 p.m.,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.020
a Norfolk Southern train derailed

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.480
in the small village of
East Palestine, Ohio,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.180
which is on the border with Pennsylvania.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.680
As soon as the derailment occurred,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.900
police and other officials
came through the town

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.650
and told people that they
had to evacuate immediately.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.490
(sirens blaring)

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.280
Monday, February 6th, Norfolk Southern

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.490
said that it would have
to breach five tanker cars

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.140
containing vinyl chloride,

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.650
to prevent a potentially
catastrophic explosion.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.855
- I honestly feel that the Palestine,

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:03.000
the police department,
the fire department,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.770
all the first responders,

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.000
they don't have the answers to give us

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.290
because I don't think they know.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.110
They're not getting the
straight answers either.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.570
- [Kris] Residents in East
Palestine and surrounding areas

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:16.200
packed the school gymnasium
Wednesday night to seek answers.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.240
- We're trying to get
information out to our citizens.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.030
Everybody's concerned, I'm concerned.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.130
But, you know, it's not
Norfolk Southern here.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.182
It's the EPA, the people who
have been working with us,

00:01:25.182 --> 00:01:28.695
trying to get our citizens
back into their homes safe.

00:01:28.695 --> 00:01:30.169
- We find it very hard to believe

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:32.420
that there is no particulate map.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.440
- It was just a big runaround.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.870
Like, I feel like a lot of
the questions that were asked

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.370
were people's rantings,

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.980
and just speaking in circles.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.510
The answers that were given

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.420
were things that we've already been told.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.640
- [Kris] Norfolk Southern
declined to send representatives

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.640
to the town hall, citing safety concerns.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.060
The railroad said it has
distributed $1.5 million directly

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.730
to more than 1,000 families,
and some businesses,

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.590
and has established a $1 million fund

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.540
available immediately to the community.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.990
One of the chemicals released
in the train derailment

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.980
was vinyl chloride,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.110
which the National Cancer Institute says

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.313
is associated with a higher
risk of liver cancer.

00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:12.540
Federal and state environmental regulators

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.970
say they're going to continue
to monitor the air quality

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.410
and water in the area,

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.110
to ensure that it's safe for citizens.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.000
- What we have discovered

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.370
through the testing and
sampling that's been done

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.113
is that very early on,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.720
you know, we have estimated,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.490
based on our sampling and
modeling, about 3500 dead fish

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.900
across that space,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.548
across those streams,
tributaries, waterways.

00:02:36.548 --> 00:02:37.560
- [Kris] The administrator

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.750
for the US Environmental Protection Agency

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.100
visited Thursday.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.473
- Let me be clear.

00:02:42.473 --> 00:02:44.400
EPA will exercise

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.660
our oversight

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.420
and our enforcement
authority under the law

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.090
to be sure we are getting the results

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.800
that the community deserves.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.360
- [Kris] So far, the EPA has said

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.540
that air monitoring has
showed no levels of concern

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.880
from chemicals released into the air.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.230
The EPA has also said

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.750
that the water is safe to
drink in East Palestine

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.000
from the municipal water facility.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.960
- This is so much bigger
than just it in the water.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.709
Our environment, our wildlife animals,

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:16.440
our farmers that have
to till their soil up.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.630
- [Kris] Many residents want
testing inside their homes,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.590
which is being done.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.820
But even when it is being done,

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.560
they're still kind of distrustful

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.453
about those results at this point.

00:03:25.393 --> 00:03:28.560
(soft staccato music)

